{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Each workload is a validation run (canonical_id). Controls are the frozen targets every adapter must resolve to; a tool that cannot represent a field exactly makes the row non-comparable.",
    "Starting controls from the design spec: Newton atol 1e-9, rtol 0, 25 iterations; event atol 1e-7; ds 1e-2, ds_min 1e-5, ds_max 2e-2. The arclength metric is JaxCont's default: state weight 1/n_state (n_state counts every unknown of the continuation vector, including collocation unknowns for periodic problems), parameter weight 1. Adapters resolve the rule to the number each tool used.",
    "Fixed-step rows come first (ds_min == ds == ds_max, adaptive false). Adaptive rows are a separate experiment.",
    "accuracy_limits are the registry metric_limits for the same run (errors against the committed reference bundles), copied here so a registry change is a visible benchmark change."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "controls": {
      "newton_atol": 1e-09,
      "newton_rtol": 0.0,
      "newton_max_iter": 25,
      "event_atol": 1e-07,
      "ds": 0.01,
      "ds_min": 1e-05,
      "ds_max": 0.02,
      "adaptive": true,
      "max_steps": 1000,
      "state_weight": "1/n_state",
      "parameter_weight": 1.0,
      "stability_every_step": true,
      "newton_criterion": "augmented-residual-2norm"
    },
    "stages": [
      "startup",
      "first_call",
      "compile",
      "warm",
      "end_to_end"
    ],
    "sampling": {
      "first_calls": 5,
      "warm_repetitions": 20,
      "untimed_warmups": 3,
      "batch_sizes": [
        1,
        8,
        32,
        128
      ],
      "timeout_seconds": 1800.0
    }
  },
  "cases": [
